CONTEXT FROM TEXTBOOK:
This figure is a tall two-column diagram tracing data through the two branches of a CLIP model up into a shared space. Each branch is a bottom-to-top stack of five dark-outlined parallelograms, each carrying a faint square grid and standing for one two-dimensional embedding slice. A vertical rule on the far left is labeled "Image encoder" and one on the far right is labeled "Text encoder." Between consecutive planes on the left, heavy black upward arrows pass four rounded boxes reading "ViT block x3"; the mirroring positions on the right carry four boxes reading "transformer block x3." On the left-hand planes the data appear as small colored markers whose shape and hue echo the depicted object: pink and blue squares, pink, purple, orange and blue circles, blue and purple triangles, and a green square, each joined to its position on the plane above by a thin dashed colored line. On the right-hand planes the same items appear instead as text strings such as "red circle," "green square," "purple triangle" and "blue triangle," linked across layers by dashed gray lines. At the top, a black arrow rises from each branch’s final plane into a filled orange disk beneath the heading "Joint embedding space." Following one colored marker upward alongside its text counterpart lets the reader watch the two modalities’ layouts drift toward a common arrangement layer by layer.

PROJECTION TYPE: axonometric
Use ordinary orthographic projection: setCameraView({ projection: 'orthographic', axisScreenAngles, heightFraction }). If the plan gives axis_screen_angles: null (a flat 2D plot/diagram), pass axisScreenAngles: null for a front-on view. Otherwise the plan does not measure per-figure angles — use a standard isometric pose: axisScreenAngles: { x: 30, z: 30 }. The source image is a PROJECTION of a 3D object: rebuild the true object — a rectangle stays a rectangle in world space — and let the camera do the projecting. Never bake the drawn parallelogram into the geometry, and never shear geometry. Omit zoom and call setCameraView after all geometry is added — the scaffold auto-fits from the projected bounding box.

ELEMENTS TO RECREATE IN 3D:
  - Left (image) branch: stack of 5 dark-outlined parallelogram planes, bottom to top, each with a faint 4x4 light-gray square grid
  - Right (text) branch: identical stack of 5 dark-outlined parallelogram planes with faint grids, same five heights as the left stack
  - Colored 2D markers scattered on each left plane: pink squares, a green square, pink/purple/orange/red/blue circles, blue and purple triangles
  - Thin dashed colored trajectory lines joining each left marker to the same concept's position on the plane above (4 segments per concept)
  - Text strings on each right plane naming the same concepts: 'red circle', 'pink circle', 'purple circle', 'orange circle', 'blue circle', 'pink square', 'green square', 'blue triangle', 'purple triangle'
  - Dashed gray trajectory lines joining each text label to its position on the plane above
  - Four heavy black upward arrows on the left between consecutive planes
  - Four rounded rectangle boxes on the left reading 'ViT block x3', one beside each left arrow
  - Four heavy black upward arrows on the right between consecutive planes
  - Four rounded rectangle boxes on the right reading 'transformer block x3', one beside each right arrow
  - Vertical rule on the far left with rotated caption 'Image encoder'
  - Vertical rule on the far right with rotated caption 'Text encoder'
  - Black arrow rising diagonally from the top-left plane into the orange disk
  - Black arrow rising diagonally from the top-right plane into the orange disk
  - Filled orange disk (joint embedding space) centered above and between the two stacks
  - Title text 'Joint embedding space' above the orange disk

GEOMETRY NOTES (world-space scale, color palette, and any formula/value needed for correctness — build to these so sizes, zoom, and colors match the source; do not guess dimensions the notes already specify):
World scale: each embedding plane is a 4.0 x 4.0 square in the XZ plane (flat, normal = +Y), outlined in dark gray #4a4a4a at ~2px, filled white/transparent, with an internal 4x4 light-gray (#dcdcdc) grid. Five planes per branch at y = 0, 2.4, 4.8, 7.2, 9.6 (bottom-to-top). Left (image) stack centered at x = -4.0, right (text) stack at x = +4.0, both at z = 0; the source offsets successive planes slightly, so shift each plane +0.35 in x per level going up for the left stack and +0.35 for the right stack to reproduce the staggered look. Orange disk: radius 0.95, filled #F4A582 with black outline, centered at (0, 12.6, 0), facing the viewer; title 'Joint embedding space' above it. Two black arrows (shaft ~0.06 thick) run from the top-left plane center (-3.0, 9.8) and top-right plane center (3.0, 9.8) diagonally inward to the disk rim. Between-plane arrows: 4 black vertical arrows on the left at x = -7.2 and 4 on the right at x = +7.2, each spanning one 2.4-unit gap; rounded-rect labels 'ViT block x3' sit at x = -6.0 and 'transformer block x3' at x = +6.0, vertically centered in each gap, white fill with black rounded border, monospace text. Far-left vertical rule at x = -9.2 spanning y = -1 to 10.6 with rotated serif caption 'Image encoder'; mirrored rule at x = +9.2 with 'Text encoder'. Nine concepts, each with a fixed color and a distinct random-walk 2D position per level (positions should jitter noticeably at low levels and converge to near-identical relative layouts across the two branches at the top two levels): red circle #E8746B, pink circle #F58CB6, purple circle #B3A4E0, orange circle #F3A76A, blue circle #5BC8E8, pink square #F776CE, green square #55C98B, blue triangle #3AAEE0, purple triangle #A79BE0. Markers on the left are ~0.16-unit sprites of the matching shape drawn in the concept color; on the right the same concept appears as small dark text (e.g. 'blue triangle') in ~0.22-unit sans-serif. Trajectory lines: left branch uses dashed lines in the concept color at ~25% opacity; right branch uses dashed gray (#555, 25% opacity). Highlighted concept draws both its left and right chains at full opacity and 2x width.

DISCRETE CONTROLS (implement every one of these in #ui, each must work independently):
